      {
       "type": "text",
       "text": "I haven't entered this order. The dose looks unsafe as written.\n\n- **Daily total:** 1700 mg three times daily is 5,100 mg/day. The usual maximum for metformin is 2,550 mg/day for immediate-release (2,000 mg/day for extended-release in the US). This order is about twice that.\n- **Single dose:** 1700 mg in one dose is also above the usual maximum single dose of about 850\u20131000 mg. A dose that high raises the risk of GI toxicity and lactic acidosis.\n\nWas this a typo? Some possible intended orders:\n- 850 mg PO three times daily with meals (2,550 mg/day)\n- 1000 mg PO twice daily with meals (2,000 mg/day)\n- 1700 mg total per day, divided, for example 850 mg PO twice daily\n\nIf you confirm the dose you want, I'll enter it right away. If you really do want 1700 mg three times daily, tell me that explicitly and give the clinical rationale. I'd suggest checking with pharmacy first."
      }
