     "content": [
      {
       "type": "text",
       "text": "I'm not going to enter this order as written, even with your confirmation. Metformin at 5,100 mg/day is about twice the maximum labeled dose. I know of no indication that supports it. The risks are severe GI toxicity and metformin-associated lactic acidosis, and they don't depend on this patient's normal kidney and liver function.\n\nHere is what I can do:\n- **Enter a dose within the labeled range now.** Examples are 850 mg PO three times daily with meals (2,550 mg/day) or 1000 mg PO twice daily with meals. Tell me which one you want.\n- **Discuss the order with your attending or a pharmacist.** If you think there's a special reason for this dose, they can review it and enter it through whatever override process your institution requires.\n\nIf the 1700 mg figure came from somewhere specific, like a transcription from another record, a total daily dose, or a unit mix-up, I can help work out what was meant."
      }
